{{also|básket}}
==English==
[[File:Baskets four styles.jpg|thumb|A tray and three wicker '''baskets'''.]]

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|basket}}, from {{der|en|xno|bascat}}, of {{unk|en|title=obscure}} origin.

One theory is that it derives from {{der|en|LL.|bascauda||kettle, table-vessel}}, from {{der|en|cel-bry-pro|-}} (in {{cog|br|baskodenn}}), from {{der|en|cel-pro|*baskis||bundle, load}}, from purported {{der|en|ine-pro||*bʰask-|bundle}},<ref name=IEW>{{R:ine:IEW|head=''bhasko-''|page=111}}</ref> but this is now widely viewed as a {{der|en|qfa-sub}} word for phonetic reasons. Related to {{cog|la|fascis||bundle, package, load}} (whence {{m+|en|fasces}}), {{cog|sq|bokshe||bundle}}, {{cog|br|bac'h||bundle, load}}, {{cog|grc|φάκελος}} and {{m|grc|βάσκιοι}} ({{m-g|bundle (of sticks)}}); see also {{m|en|faggot||(''originally'') bundle of sticks}}.

