===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# A lightweight container, generally round, open at the top, and tapering toward the bottom.
#: {{ux|en|A '''basket''' of fake fruit adorned the table.}}
## {{lb|en|by extension}} A [[bed]] for a [[cat]].
# A wire or plastic container similar in shape to a basket, used for carrying articles for purchase in a shop.
# {{lb|en|internet}} In an [[online]] [[shop]], a listing of a customer's chosen [[item]]s before they are [[order]]ed.
# {{lb|en|figurative}} A set or collection of intangible things.
#* '''2004''', Gichinga Ndirangu, Heinrich Böll Foundation (Nairobi, Kenya), ''An African civil society action toward WTO 2003'' (page 16)
#*: The '''basket''' of issues that developing countries had vigorously wanted addressed such as agriculture, SANDD and implementation-related issues were given scant attention by developed countries for most part of the conference.
# {{lb|en|basketball}} A circular hoop, from which a net is suspended, which is the goal through which the players try to throw the ball.
#: {{ux|en|The point guard drove toward the '''basket'''.}}
# {{lb|en|basketball}} The act of putting the ball through the basket, thereby scoring points.
#: {{ux|en|The last-second '''basket''' sealed the victory.}}
# {{lb|en|uncountable}} The game of [[basketball]].
#: {{ux|en|Let's play some '''basket'''.}}
# A dance movement in some line dances, where men put their arms round the women's lower backs, and the women put their arms over the men's shoulders, and the group (usually of four, any more is difficult) spins round, which should result in the women's feet leaving the ground.
# {{lb|en|LGBTQ|slang}} The [[penis]] and region surrounding it.<ref name="Niemoeller"/>
# {{lb|en|slang}} The bulge of the penis seen through clothing.
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} In a [[stage-coach]], two outside seats facing each other.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1773|author=w:Oliver Goldsmith|title=s:She Stoops to Conquer
|passage=In my time, the follies of the town crept slowly among us, but now they travel faster than a stage-coach. Its fopperies come down not only as inside passengers, but in the very '''basket'''.}}
# {{lb|en|archaic}} A protection for the hand on a sword or a [[singlestick]]; a [[guard]] of a bladed weapon.
## A [[singlestick]] with a basket hilt.
##* {{quote-text|en|year=1773|author=w:Oliver Goldsmith|title=s:She Stoops to Conquer
|passage=Baw! damme, but I'll fight you both, one after the other——with '''baskets'''.}}
# {{lb|en|ballooning}} The gondola or wicker basket suspended from the balloon, in which the pilot and passengers travel.
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2013-06-07|author=David Simpson
|volume=188|issue=26|page=36|magazine=w:The Guardian Weekly
|title=[http://www.guardian.co.uk/books/2013/may/18/falling-upwards-richard-holmes-review Fantasy of navigation]
|passage=Like most human activities, ballooning has sponsored heroes and hucksters and a good deal in between. For every dedicated scientist patiently recording atmospheric pressure and wind speed while shivering at high altitudes, there is a carnival barker with a bevy of pretty girls willing to dangle from a '''basket''' or parachute down to earth.}}
# {{lb|en|architecture}} The [[bell]] or [[vase]] of the [[Corinthian]] [[capital]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1832|author=Edward Hall|title=Civil Architecture|passage=Thus the capital of the Corinthian column always resembles a deep narrow '''basket''' covered with a tile, and completely surrounded by foliage}}
# {{lb|en|informal|euphemism}} [[bastard|Bastard]].
#: {{ux|en|Wait till I catch you, you little '''basket'''!}}
# {{lb|en|military|aircraft}} A [[drogue]] (or para-drogue) in the probe-and-drogue refueling method
#: {{ux|en|Don't smoosh the '''basket'''.}}

